  "type": "MULTIPLE_CHOICE",
  "data": {
    "body": "We are given two series with positive terms $S_1=\\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty}a_k$ and $S_2=\\sum_{k=1}^{\\infty}b_k$, and we further know that \\[\\lim_{k\\to\\infty}\\frac{a_{k+1}}{a_k}=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{ and }\\lim_{k\\to\\infty}\\frac{b_k}{a_k}=2\\] What can we say about the convergence of these two series based on the given information?",
    "solution": [
      3
    ],
    "answerChoices": [
      {
        "id": "e3275ab9-6431-4996-8ad7-41e4dd864b65",
        "index": 0,
        "body": "$S_1$ must be convergent but $S_2$ could be convergent or divergent",
        "questionId": "8e2a3ec6-d294-41c0-a6f4-a6f49250985e",
